export anchor EsportsBroadcastStyle:
    number: 315
    screen: OpsMonitor
    name: Esports broadcast
    idea: The monitor as a live broadcast overlay, with a LIVE bug, a slanted scoreboard where each service is a team with its own colour and its uptime as the score, a big stage chart with a lower third for the incident, and tickers of alerts and deploys.
    base: dark
    palette:
        arena: #090c18, the page under a soft navy spotlight gradient at the top
        stage: #11162a, the chart stage, desk cards and the style sheet
        bar: #1a2142, scoreboard blocks, tickers and the title bar
        barRaised: #232b52, the current app tab and the lower third action area
        ink: #ffffff, text, and section tags drawn as white blocks with dark text
        muted: #b0b8db, labels, times and axis ticks
        line: #2d3663, card borders, rules and grid lines
        live: #d6193a, the LIVE bug and the incident key in the lower third, with white text
        highlight: #ffe066, the request line, the peak pin, the primary button, ticker labels and focus
        teamApi: #4da3ff, api team tag and score underline
        teamWeb: #ff9d3c, web team tag and score underline
        teamSync: #2fd8c4, sync-worker team tag, score underline and the p50 line
        teamNotif: #b893ff, notifications team tag, score underline and the p95 line
        teamBilling: #ffd84a, billing team tag and score underline
        healthy: #6ee7a0, Healthy and Resolved with filled circle and square
        degraded: #ffcf4a, Degraded and Investigating with triangle and magnifier
        recovered: #86cfff, Recovered with a filled diamond
        firing: #ff8593, Firing with a filled octagon and the error line
    type:
        Segoe UI, Helvetica Neue, Roboto, Arial, mostly italic at 800 to
        900. Base 15px at 1.45. Scores are 28px italic 900 with tabular
        numbers and a smaller percent sign, the lower third title 20px
        italic 900, section tags 13px italic 900 caps tracked 0.14em, small
        caps meta 12px at 800.
    layout:
        A broadcast top bar made of skewed blocks, a red LIVE bug with a
        white dot, then a navy title block with Brightwork Ops and
        Production last 24 hours, and the suite apps at right with a yellow
        underline on Ops. A white skewed tag reads Scoreboard uptime above a
        row of five parallelogram team blocks skewed 14 degrees with upright
        text. Each block has a team colour three letter tag such as API or
        SYN, the service name, the uptime as a large italic score, and a
        footer with the status word and shape and one fact, and a 4px team
        colour underline. billing shows 6 MIN DOWN as its score. Below sits
        the arena, a wide stage with a Requests per minute tag, a peak
        readout, a yellow area line chart with a 9,400 pin, and across its
        foot a lower third with a red INCIDENT key, a pale caption panel
        holding INC-0427 sync-worker queue backlog with severity, opened,
        owner and Investigating, and an Open incident button. Beside the
        stage a 320px caster desk holds Error rate and Latency cards with
        coloured top edges. At the foot, two ticker rows with yellow Alerts
        and Deploys labels list items in segments. Below 1100px the desk
        moves under the stage, below 760px blocks lose their skew and stack
        and tickers become lists.
    spacing: An 8px unit. 24px gutter, 16px between stage and desk, 10px between scoreboard blocks, 16px ticker segment padding.
    density: Medium. Five big scores on top, one big stage, two desk cards and two ticker rows.
    corners: None. Blocks are parallelograms skewed 14 degrees and the primary button is a clipped slant.
    borders: A 4px team colour underline per score block, 4px colour tops on desk cards, a 2px highlight rule over each ticker.
    shadows: None. Depth comes from a navy spotlight gradient behind everything.
    icons:
        Filled status shapes beside the word, a circle for Healthy, a
        triangle for Degraded, a diamond for Recovered, an octagon for
        Firing, a square for Resolved and a magnifier for Investigating.
        Teams are three letter codes, deploys use an upload arrow.
    focus: A 3px highlight yellow outline offset 3px. Slanted buttons drop their clip while focused so the ring shows.
    tone: Broadcast captions in italic caps such as LIVE, Scoreboard uptime, INCIDENT and Peak 9,400.
